      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Magic-angle twisted bilayer graphene revealed tunable flat bands with correlated insulating and superconducting phases, opening a major new direction in quantum materials.",
        "attribution": "Bistritzer and MacDonald supplied the key theoretical prediction of flat bands, while Jarillo-Herrero's group established the striking correlated phenomena experimentally.",
        "maturity": "The central results have been studied extensively, but the mechanisms and relation among observed phases remain active research questions.",
